BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Winter Magic
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261130T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261130T180000
UID:261116YQnbt9RPK0i8IdvLYvqTAw
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  11/15/26\n\nDECEMBER EXHIBIT: WI
 NTER MAGIC\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  November 23– December 27\, 2026\n\nRECEPT
 ION/HOLIDAY OPEN HOUSE: DECEMBER 5\, 2026\, 11am to 6pm: Join in to meet t
 he artists and cheer the season\, the show and enjoy holiday goodies. As p
 art of the festivities\, we will host our monthly free drawing for an artw
 ork by Ron Sumner.  The Gallery is pleased to participate again this year
  in the Healdsburg Chamber’s Holiday Sip & Shop – for more information
 : 2026 Healdsburg Holiday Sip & Shop\, Eventbrite.com.\n\nSonoma County ar
 tists\, Willow LaLand\, Phyllis Rapp\, Linda Loveland Reid\, Laura Roney\,
  Luba Stolper\, Ron Sumner\, Jo Tobin-Charleston\, Carolyn Wilson and Gen 
 Zorich present Winter Magic\, a mix of unique artistic expressions creatin
 g a magical welcome to the 2026 holiday season.  Starting with nature’s
  magic -the colorful painterly skies at dawn and dusk – LaLand’s “Bo
 ston Harbor” at sunrise engenders warm feelings of hope as does Roney’
 s “Dancing in the Snow” in the waning rays of daylight.  Stolper weav
 es a spell with “Whispering Elegance\,” objects so real – the lace\,
  the cherries\, the vase- the viewer is drawn in awe.  Wilson’s “New 
 Beginnings” draws the viewer’s eye with lively colorful flowers that s
 eem to dance for joy.  Artists Rapp and Sumner turn to our feline and fea
 thered friends for inspiration:  in Rapp’s “Emerald Eye\,” the kitt
 y captivates us with a mesmerizing gaze and Sumner’s “Snowy Owl” loo
 ks out from its perch in a moonlit snowy glen.   From our abstract artis
 ts\, Reid lights our spirit with “Green for Joy” and Zorich’s “Lay
 ers and Red Rock\, “compelling in texture with splashes of random color 
 shapes. To enable us to cast one’s own spell\, Tobin-Charleston’s spar
 kle/colored-themed crystal pendant sets are the perfect ticket.\n\nAll mem
 ber artists are showing many smaller works throughout the Gallery\, ideal 
 for gifting.\n\nFor the Holiday Season our Staircase Showcase features man
 y different hand-crafted 3D artist offerings. Ceramic artists Kathy Brown\
 , Joann Cassady\, Ed Price\, Karen Norton and Steve Sanders offer a variet
 y of vases\, platters\, and bowls.  Our glass artists\, Brian & Nancy Rob
 erts\, Melissa McCann and Tim Montesouti present gorgeous fused glass art\
 , decorative boxes\, and tree ornaments. Plus\, we have horsehair bowls an
 d decorated gourds by Susan Miron and wooden bird sculptures presented by 
 Amber Biocca. And\, as always\, there is jewelry throughout the gallery. Y
 ou can find the perfect earrings\, necklace\, pendant or bracelet from our
  local jewelers: Galley-member Jo Tobin-Charleston\, Aaron Poovey\, Laura 
 Buckner\, Melissa McCann\, Patricia Reilly\, Hamida Judith Dides\, Elaine 
 Greene\, Heyoka Merrifield\, and JoAnna Noble.\n\nJOIN US for ARTNITE HEAL
 DSBURG\, THURSDAY\, DECEMBER 3  5:00 – 7:00 pm : Artnite Healdsburg is 
 a community event celebrating art and creativity with more than 20 galleri
 es participating\, along with select restaurants\, bars and boutiques. \n
 \nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707
 \\) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm\; extended holiday hours: Open Fr
 i & Sat 10am – 7pm through December 23rd\; closed December 25.    www
 .upstairsartgallery.net \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird
 \, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
