BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:SSU Symphonic Wind Ensemble 25th Anniversary
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T193000
UID:26112094qrtqGHQkOESQImPedP5A
DESCRIPTION:Help us celebrate the 25th anniversary of the Sonoma State Uni
 versity Symphonic Wind Ensemble with a program of chosen gems for wind ban
 d!\n\nFounded by Dr. Brian Wilson in 2001\, and under the leadership of co
 nductor Dr. Andy Collinsworth since 2008\, the Symphonic Wind Ensemble has
  gained widespread acclaim for its outstanding performances of contemporar
 y and traditional wind repertoire. Comprised of the finest woodwind\, bras
 s\, and percussion performers at the university\, the Symphonic Wind Ensem
 ble embraces musical artistry and collaboration\, and endeavors to engage\
 , connect\, and inspire audiences in the university\, educational\, and No
 rth Bay communities.\n\nThe SWE has collaborated with some of the leading 
 contemporary composers including Viet Cuong\, Paul Dooley\, Shuying Li\, J
 ohn Mackey\, Oscar Navarro\, James Stephenson\, and in March 2027\, compos
 er Michael Daugherty will be in residence.\n\nThe ensemble performs freque
 ntly throughout the year at university concerts and festivals and has perf
 ormed on tour at locations throughout the West. The SWE has twice been inv
 ited to perform at the College Band Directors National Association (CBDNA)
  Western-Northwestern Division Conference.
LOCATION:Green Music Center - Weill Hall
URL:https://music.sonoma.edu/events/symphonic-wind-ensemble-25th-anniversa
 ry?utm_source=sonoma_calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall
 _2026_symphonic_wind_25th_anniversary
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
