BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marin Farmers Markets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T130000
UID:261128ldeTaOGBkkOa0suDUnN4hg
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free\n\nSponsor: Marin Center\n\nWe are hosting our ann
 ual pie backing contest at the farmers market\,Thursday Pie Baking Contest
  RSVP\n\nExplore the bounty of summer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste 
 vine-ripened tomatoes\, corn that was picked that morning\, an d peaches s
 o juicy you have to bend over just to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-
 fed beef\, artisan cheeses\, raw milk\, and freshly baked b reads complete
  the shopping experience. Specialty prepared foods and handmade art add to
  the magic of the market.\n\nEnjoy the intimate feeling of the Thursday Ma
 rin Farmers Market\, an ideal place to meet for lunch and pick up fresh pr
 oduce for the weekend. Discover the abundance and diversity of product at 
 the celebrated Sunday Marin Farmers Market\, the third largest farmers mar
 ket in California. Turn your dollar into a vote for local sustainable agri
 culture\, shrink your eco-footprint\, and revi ve the feeling of being int
 imately connected to your food by meeting your farmers face-to-face. The m
 arket takes place rain or shine.\n\nwww.aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin Veterans' Memorial Auditorium
URL:https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261203T170000
UID:261004YzKscJFmDEqNMPu15j6Nsg
DESCRIPTION:EAMES & EAMES: Meet the couple who Defined Modern Design\n\nCr
 eated in collaboration with the Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.\n\n
 EAMES & EAMES explores the iterative\, hands-on\, and human-centered appr
 oach of Charles & Ray Eames. Through furniture\, toys\, paintings\, graphi
 cs\, and personal belongings collected over their lifetimes\, this groundb
 reaking exhibition looks beyond the iconic Eames chairs to reveal the brea
 dth of their creative practice. More than any single object\, their work o
 pened doors to new and unexpected ways of seeing\, thinking\, making\, and
  understanding the world—ideas that continue to inspire us today.\n\nCur
 ated by Llisa Demetrios\, Co-Founder & The Lucia Eames Chief Curator of th
 e Eames Institute of Infinite Curiosity.
LOCATION:The MAC - Napa Valley Museum of Art & Culture
URL:https://napavalleymuseum.org/blogs/upcoming-exhibitions/eames-eames
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
