BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dirty Cello at Mac's at 19 Broadway
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T220000
UID:26112605PfvONN2Eanp0HyjVrx5w
DESCRIPTION:'Tis the season to hear way too much holiday music!\n\nJoin th
 e band Dirty Cello for an evening of wild blues\, rock and Americana with 
 little to know Christmas music. Give your ears a break from Mariah Carey\,
  and come out for some Zeppelin\, Stevie Ray\, and Rolling Stones.\n\nThe 
 band Dirty Cello plays all over the world from Iceland to Singapore and th
 ey love performing in their hometown of Marin County. Join this world trav
 eling band for a special show at Mac’s at 19 Broadway.\n\nOn Dec 5 at 8 
 pm\, Dirty Cello will perform a concert of wild rock and roll\, soulful bl
 ues and irreverent originals performed with high energy abandon. The group
  has been described by the L.A. Times as\, "The group seamlessly careens f
 rom blues to bluegrass and rock in a way that really shouldn't make sense 
 but somehow does."\n\nMac’s at 19 Broadway opened in 1926 and has turned
  from a dive bar into an upscale prohibition-style lounge.\n\nTickets are 
 available at the door\, but pre-bought tickets are preferred.
LOCATION:Mac's at
URL:https://macsat19broadway.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hidden Gems of the North Bay Opening Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T210000
UID:261124vAPyS9Mf60mx5VSPj0A55A
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the opening reception of "Hidden Gems of the North
  Bay"\, our featured holiday exhibition by Marin photographer Jeff Lewis. 
 Enjoy jazzy live music by The Hot Clams\, delicious refreshments and wine\
 , and cozy holiday shopping.\n\nJeff is a full-time professional landscape
  photographer and light wizard with over a decade’s experience behind th
 e camera. With his partner Tung\, he specializes in custom-created\, ultra
 -high-resolution images that are ready to display in large prints and digi
 tal applications that demand perfect detail. “Hidden Gems of the North B
 ay” will highlight his work around the Bay Area \n\n"Hidden Gems of the
  North Bay" will be featured at Usher Gallery from November 24 to January 
 10.
LOCATION:Usher Gallery
URL:https://ushergallerypetaluma.com/blogs/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
