DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T170000
UID:261123MJ5f_egcSkGuaZIICXUp9A
DESCRIPTION:Jack’s Bookshop at Jack London State Historic Park will host
  a special “Deck the Shelves: Member Appreciation Day” on Saturday\, D
 ec. 5\, at 10 a.m. to 5 p.m.   Those with park memberships\, including t
 hose who become members that day\, will receive a 20% discount on all in-p
 erson purchases (membership and park entrance fees not included).  The fi
 rst 40 members to visit and make a purchase will receive a complimentary b
 randed tote bag.\n\nJack’s Bookshop\, inside the House of Happy Walls Mu
 seum\, features museum-editions of the complete works of Jack London\, one
  of the most successful writers of the 20th century whose stories continue
  to engage readers of all ages around the world. His most famous novel\, 
 “The Call of the Wild\,” for example\, is available in versions for ag
 es 7 to adults.  \n\nJack's Bookshop also offers titles authored by Charm
 ian London\, his wife\, and various biographies that give insight into the
 ir adventurous lives.  Jack’s Bookshop also carries apparel\, stationer
 y\, and souvenirs that make the perfect holiday gifts for nature and book 
 lovers alike. New t-shirts\, sweatshirts\, hats\, and tote bags are now av
 ailable\, all made in collaboration with local screenprinting studio Sonom
 a Ink. \n\nAnnual memberships to the park make excellent gifts.  Startin
 g at $59\, membership includes a pass for entry to the park all year for t
 he pass holder and up to nine passengers in a private vehicle.  The regul
 ar entry fee is $15 per vehicle.  The annual membership pass is also vali
 d for entrance to Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, just eight miles away in Ke
 nwood\, CA. \n\nBooks and other items can be ordered online at https://ja
 cklondonpark.com/jacks-shop/all-items/ (the Dec. 15 discount does not appl
 y to online orders). All purchases support the non-profit Jack London Park
  Partners\, which funds and operates the park.  Passes can also be ordere
 d online and will be mailed to the giver or the recipient.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/jacks-shop/all-items/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
