BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bright Nights at Cuvaison
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T190000
UID:261115dgw890DXGEqnOdlOW_oldg
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the magic of the holiday season with Bright Nights\,
  an evening wine tasting experience set against one of Cuvaison’s most e
 nchanting backdrops: rows and rows of estate vineyards illuminated with tw
 inkling lights.\n\nOffered Friday\, Saturday\, and Sunday evenings from No
 vember 27 through January 3\, Bright Nights invites you to experience the 
 beauty of wine country after dark as the vineyard comes alive with a warm 
 holiday glow. From 5:00pm to 7:00pm\, settle in for a cozy seasonal tastin
 g featuring a selection of Cuvaison wines served with seasonal cheese and 
 charcuterie pairing.\n\nWhether you’re gathering with friends\, celebrat
 ing the season\, or creating a new holiday tradition\, Bright Nights offer
 s a festive and memorable way to enjoy the estate.\n\nExperience Highlight
 s:\n\n·         Rows of estate vineyards illuminated with twinkli
 ng holiday lights\n\n·         Curated wine and cheese pairings\n
 \n·         Festive evening tasting from 5:00pm to 7:00pm\n\n· 
         A magical seasonal setting for friends and holiday gatherin
 gs\n\nThis special tasting experience is offered Fridays\, Saturdays and S
 undays from November 27 through January 3\, with reservations beginning at
  5:00\, 5:15\, and 5:30pm. Please include all guests in your reservation.\
 n\nCuvaison and Brandlin Estate members receive preferred pricing and will
  see a $35 discount for up to 4 guests applied at checkout. Please use the
  email address where you receive membership updates in order for your disc
 ount to apply.\n\nCuvaison kindly asks that all guests be 21 years of age 
 or older to enjoy this experience \\(unless otherwise noted for special fa
 mily friendly dates\\). The patio is closed during Bright Nights\, so Cuva
 ison is not able to accommodate pets.\n\nImportant Dates:\n\nThursday\, No
 vember 12 – Industry Event\n\nSaturday\, November 15 – Member Pick-up 
 Event \\+ Holiday Shopping\n\nFriday\, November 27 – Bright Nights Launc
 h \\+ Black Friday Specials\n\nThursday\, December 3 – Bright Nights Wor
 kshop event\n\nSunday\, December 13 – Bright Nights Family Night \\(incl
 udes milk \\+ cookie pairing for kids\, and a holiday activity\\). This ev
 ening may also include a photographer offering Holiday Family portraits.\n
 \nSunday\, December 27 – Bright Nights Family Night \\(includes milk \\+
  cookie pairing for kids\, and a holiday activity\\). This evening may als
 o include a photographer offering Holiday Family portraits.
LOCATION:Cuvaison Estate Tasting Room
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paul Steward (Matinée)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261205T160000
UID:261115VnNbx_sp_0-ny6mNQ_kRPQ
DESCRIPTION:$15 General Admission\n\nDoors at 4:00pm. \n\nShow from 4:45-7
 :00pm with one intermission\n\nPaul Steward is an award-winning singer and
  guitarist hailing from the San Francisco Bay Area. For over two decades\,
  he has fronted the band Twice As Good as its lead vocalist and guitarist.
  His 2022 solo debut album earned him the nickname "the world champion\," 
 propelling him on tours across the U.S. and internationally. Paul’s musi
 c fuses Blues\, R&B\, Pop\, and Native American sounds—a heartfelt tribu
 te to his Elem Pomo tribal roots. Inspired by legends like B.B. King\, Rob
 ert Randolph\, Al Green\, and Bruno Mars\, he delivers powerful\, soulful 
 vocals paired with smooth\, melodic guitar lines that keep crowds dancing.
  His artistry has earned him multiple honors\, including the 2010 Native A
 merican Music Award\, 2010 West Coast Blues Hall of Fame Award\, 2013 Indi
 an Summer Music Award\, the 2016 NorBay Music Award\, and the 2023 Yerba B
 uena Center for the Arts Honors.\n\nhttps://paul2xg.com/ https://www.faceb
 ook.com/paul2xg https://www.instagram.com/paul2xg https://www.youtube.com/
 @paul2xg\n\nRecommended If You Like: Tommy Castro\, Stevie Ray Vaughan\, G
 ary Clarke Jr
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket#/instances/a0FUh0
 0000EK3OHMA1
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
