BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Muunjuun & Sakoyana
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T203000
UID:261127ZvbQhZi3E0iVWuEZnMXtQQ
DESCRIPTION:**A cosmic funk dance party in West County: Sakoyana\, Muunjuu
 n’s first full-band show. Plus DJ Bankshot.**\n\nCome ready to move.\n\n
 Three acts\, one long night of groove at The Forestville Club\, for fans o
 f Khruangbin\, Vulfpeck\, Thundercat and Parliament-Funkadelic.\n\nSakoyan
 a is a Sonoma County band that can turn on a dime from tight\, horn-sharp 
 grooves into wide-open jams. Think Snarky Puppy at a backyard party: the k
 ind of set that makes the drummer grin and the whole room bounce.\n\nMuunj
 uun {MOON-june} plays music that feels like tripping without the mushrooms
 . Bootsy Collins called him a “west coast cosmic funktroid.” This is h
 is first show with the full five-piece band\, so expect warm\, wobbly\, sk
 y-high pop-funk that pulls you onto the floor and keeps you there.\n\nDJ B
 ankshot keeps the floor moving between sets\, so there’s no reason to si
 t down.\n\nFriday\, December 11th · 8:30 PM The Forestville Club · Fores
 tville\, CA $20 · advance tickets $25 · at the door *Limited capacity* 2
 1+
LOCATION:The Forestville Club
URL:https://www.muunjuun.com/shop/p/sakoyana-muunjuun-live-at-the-forestvi
 lle-club-dec-11
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261211T235900
UID:261124lP9ubT8NdUaaIAvoIPln4Q
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women \\(NLAPW\\) and the 
 Golden Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over
  18 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional
  and national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-fina
 list phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Na
 tional competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and ha
 ve their entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invit
 ed to present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become 
 semi-finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to thre
 e winners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published
  in The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed
  in the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee 
 of $15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrict
 ions on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 
 25\, 2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatema
 rinart.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org
URL:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
