DESCRIPTION:Garrett Hardware invites families to join us every second Satu
 rday from **9:00 AM to 11:00 AM** for our monthly Kid’s Activity Day at 
 **both our Windsor and Healdsburg stores.** For just **$10 per child**\, k
 ids can enjoy a hands-on DIY experience where they’ll build seasonal pro
 jects like March’s Leprechaun Catchers\, April’s garden crafts\, and M
 ay’s handmade Mother’s Day gifts. Our team provides all the materials 
 and guidance needed\, ensuring every child leaves with a sense of pride an
 d a finished project they built themselves. It is a fantastic\, affordable
  way for kids to learn new skills while parents enjoy a stress-free mornin
 g of community and creativity.
LOCATION:Garrett Hardware
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/garrett-hardware-kid-s-
 activity-day/18163623/2026-12-12T09
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Overeaters Anonymous (OA) Newcomer Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T094500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T101500
UID:260212IiHNpXS6f0e-rmk1S99Wzw
DESCRIPTION:Is Food a Problem for You? You Are Not Alone.\n\nOvereaters An
 onymous \\(OA\\) is a fellowship of people who support each other in recov
 ering from compulsive eating and food behaviors. If you feel you have a pr
 oblem with food\, OA welcomes you—no matter what your background\, belie
 fs\, or eating habits. \n\nWe hold an in-person newcomer meeting on first
 \, second and fourth Saturdays of the month from 9:45 - 10:15 AM at ​Uni
 tarian Universalist Congregation of Marin\, 240 Channing Way\, San Rafael 
 CA 94903. Contact: Sue M. 415-298-6792​. You may view all North Bay OA 
 in-person and online meetings at https://www.northbayoa.org/meetings.html\
 n\nIn OA\, members experience spiritual\, emotional\, and physical recover
 y by practicing the Twelve Steps and living by their spiritual principles
 —one day at a time.\n\nOA is not a diet club or calorie-counting program
 .\n\nMembers have different plans of eating.\n\nOA does not endorse any sp
 ecific food plan. \n\nIf food is causing problems in your life\, you don
 ’t have to struggle alone. Recovery is possible\, and help is available.
 \n\nVisit: https://www.northbayoa.org/\n\nFind a meeting: https://www.nort
 hbayoa.org/meetings.html
LOCATION:Unitarian Universalist Congregation of Marin
URL:https://www.northbayoa.org/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MovingWriting: Embodied Expressive Writing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T170000
UID:260129mIiKW4t1qUi6TBkMOfptlg
DESCRIPTION:In *MovingWriting* workshops\, we play with movement/dance a
 nd words to help us connect with our deep and creative selves in the compa
 ny of a supportive circle. Giving voice to our own stories and witnessing 
 the stories of others brings healing\, aliveness\, and connection with oth
 ers.\n\nNo moving or writing experience necessary!\n\nHere's what a few re
 cent *MovingWriting* participants had to say about their experience:\n\n
 “Loretta's well-crafted writing prompts sparked a writer inside me that 
 I didn't know I had… I left feeling invigorated\, accomplished and proud
  of myself for trying something new.”\n\n“I'm neither a writer nor a d
 ancer\, but Loretta made it easy to put aside my inhibitions and let my em
 otional body lead the way… I recommend this class for anybody at all!”
 \n\n"It felt delicious to dive into my creative moving and language self w
 ith others. For days after\, I felt both emptied and filled up creatively 
 in ways that I hadn’t felt in a long time."\n\n"I felt refreshed\, renew
 ed\, and like I had processed some emotional blockages… The paths were o
 pened and the words just flowed."\n\nCome move and write with us! Visit ww
 w.MovingWriting.com to learn more & register for upcoming events.
LOCATION:A private studio in Sebastopol
URL:http://www.MovingWriting.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
