BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aeternum Choir Performance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261214T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261214T190000
UID:260819I07hlYZwFEyRIvRf_qkzVg
DESCRIPTION:Known for its blend of precision and warmth\, the group create
 s immersive musical experiences that highlight the power of the human voic
 e. The choir brings together skilled singers with a shared commitment to m
 usical excellence and collaborative artistry. Their repertoire often spans
  early sacred music\, contemporary works\, and thoughtfully curated progra
 ms that explore thematic connections across time and style. Emphasizing cl
 arity of tone\, balance\, and emotional depth\, the ensemble strives to co
 mmunicate the text and spirit of each piece with authenticity and nuance. 
 Through both traditional concert settings and innovative presentations\, A
 eternum Choir engages audiences with performances that are at once refined
 \, evocative\, and deeply resonant.
LOCATION:D
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/aeternum-choir-performance/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jumpstart Your Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261214T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261214T160000
UID:260629iTDcLxVpe0O_gjhC8UEkHQ
DESCRIPTION:Every person experiences an ebb and flow to the tides of their
  creativity. We will share space together to design\, exchange ideas\, and
  hold ourselves accountable to our unique interests! The first portion of 
 our time together will involve a check-in discussion of ‘what is'\, lead
 ing into ‘what could be'. The talk will be facilitated by Erin Partridge
 \, an art therapist with a long history of supporting people in reengaging
  with creativity. After our initial talk\, we will have some time to indiv
 idually focus on our creative practices in the space of the gallery. Befor
 e we close\, we will share anything that came up in the process. Bring you
 r ideas\, a project\, and an interest in creative community. Please be min
 dful of what you choose to show up with-something quiet\, easy to clean up
 \, and non-disruptive to your fellow creatives. Not sure where to begin? S
 ome basic materials are available\, thanks to a donation from  Blick Art M
 aterials . Open for all ages-youth under 12 with an adult chaperone please
 ! Mondays\, 1-4 PM Facilitator: Erin Partridge
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/jumpstart-your-art/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
