BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261217T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261217T235900
UID:261124sm-wFY3ZHEK4k-Xmah7qeQ
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women \\(NLAPW\\) and the 
 Golden Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over
  18 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional
  and national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-fina
 list phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Na
 tional competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and ha
 ve their entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invit
 ed to present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become 
 semi-finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to thre
 e winners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published
  in The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed
  in the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee 
 of $15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrict
 ions on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 
 25\, 2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatema
 rinart.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org
URL:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
