BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet the Maker with Winemaker Jeff Mangahas of Williams Selyem
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T193000
UID:261127mG0A_bU1OU20sI4HCOxakg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special evening with Winemaker Jeff Mangahas of 
 Williams Selyem\, one of Sonoma County's most celebrated wineries and a tr
 ue pioneer of Russian River Valley Pinot Noir!\n\nWhat began in a small ga
 rage in 1979 with two friends\, Burt Williams and Ed Selyem\, has grown in
 to one of California's most respected wine brands. Today\, Jeff Mangahas c
 arries on that remarkable legacy\, bringing his background in science\, pa
 ssion for exceptional vineyards\, and thoughtful approach to winemaking to
  every vintage. Jeff's own journey with Williams Selyem began with a singl
 e glass of their Pinot Noir that inspired him to leave his career in resea
 rch and pursue winemaking.\n\nJoin Jeff and our team for an evening of gre
 at wine and conversation as he takes you behind the scenes of Williams Sel
 yem\, sharing the stories\, passion\, and craftsmanship that have shaped o
 ne of Sonoma County’s most celebrated wineries.\n\nYour tasting experien
 ce includes:\n\n\\- A special selection of four Williams Selyem wines\n\n\
 \- Deliciously paired food bites\n\n\\- The opportunity to meet Jeff\, ask
  questions\, and hear firsthand about the wines and the winery's incredibl
 e history\n\nIt's a wonderful opportunity to experience one of Sonoma Coun
 ty's most iconic wineries in a relaxed\, personal setting at Region. Seati
 ng will be limited for this exclusive event.
LOCATION:Region.
URL:https://www.exploretock.com/regionsonoma/event/630131/meet-the-maker-w
 ith-williams-selyem-winemaker-jeff-mangahas
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T235900
UID:261124ou7S4K4KnkKrKUEWvZG6kw
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women \\(NLAPW\\) and the 
 Golden Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over
  18 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional
  and national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-fina
 list phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Na
 tional competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and ha
 ve their entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invit
 ed to present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become 
 semi-finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to thre
 e winners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published
  in The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed
  in the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee 
 of $15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrict
 ions on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 
 25\, 2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatema
 rinart.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org
