BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bella Rayne
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T203000
UID:2611116rn_uyeeg0mxVVfWlBQ6VA
DESCRIPTION:MEET BELLA RAYNE | GUITARIST\n\n18 year old Bella Rayne is a s
 elf-taught guitarist\, vocalist\, and songwriter\, born in the mountains o
 f North Carolina and raised in coastal Mendocino\, California\, whose bold
  blend of jam band energy\, Southern-tinged rock\, ’90s grunge grit\, an
 d psychedelic spirit is rapidly capturing attention across the U.S. \n\nHe
 r journey began during the pandemic\, when boredom led her to resurrect an
  old Stratocaster she found in her garage. She fixed it up\, learned to pl
 ay by ear\, and quickly found her voice — melding influences from rock\,
  Americana\, bluegrass\, and the jam-band legacy into something deeply her
  own.                                              \n\nDespite her young a
 ge\, Bella has already shared the stage with seasoned artists and respecte
 d bands. Appearances alongside Allman Betts Family Revival\, Melvin Seals 
 & JGB\, ALO\, Jackie Greene\, Oteil Burbridge\, and members of Terrapin Fa
 mily have all added to her early résumé PLUS she was touted as “one to
  watch” by her idol\, Susan Tedeschi in Guitar World Magazine.\n\nOne of
  the most iconic moments of her rising career: she was entrusted to play t
 he legendary guitar known as “Alligator” — once wielded by Jerry Gar
 cia. That honor\, courtesy of Grateful Guitars Foundation\, has become a d
 efining chapter in Bella’s journey. \n\nBella has formed her own project
 \, Bella Rayne Band — a high-energy\, guitar-driven ensemble featuring a
  young lineup of seasoned musicians. Their sets are a blend of soulful Sou
 thern-rock\, modern Americana and Grateful Dead reinterpretations plus the
 ir own originals\, earning increasing demand across venues and festivals.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/109108802?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:IRA SUMMER headlines Friday Night Comedy - Downtown Santa Rosa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T220000
UID:261107bjfSehKm5UaIqmf3VBZ23Q
DESCRIPTION:Friday night stand-up comedy in Downtown Santa Rosa with headl
 iner Ira Summer\n\nVIP TABLES NOW AVAILABLE! Snag a table for 4 with prefe
 rred seating\, your own private call button to summon service\, and your f
 irst round of beer/cider (or a bottle of wine) for only $95!\n\nEvery Frid
 ay night hilarious comedians from The Bay Area and beyond perform at Barre
 l Proof Lounge. Stick around after for late-night karaoke! Fresh lineup of
  funny each Friday.\n\nThis Week: Host: Josh Argyle Lyss McGhee Steven Asi
 fo\n\nHeadliner: Ira Summer\n\nIra Summer is so funny\, you don't realize 
 that his material is clean. He uses his pain to make you laugh. As an agin
 g Baby Boomer growing up in a large dysfunctional family\, Ira has a lot t
 o share. He appreciates his sons\, siblings and mother because without the
 m\, he would have to write all of his own material.\n\nIra has headlined a
 t clubs across the United States\, performed at clubs\, casinos\, colleges
  and bars in 28 states\, and can be heard on Sirius XM. He has been a fina
 list in the The World Series of Comedy and The US Comedy Contest\, was the
  winner of the first Over 60 Comedy Competition. Ira participated in the O
 akland Comedy Festival\, the Comedy Fringe Festival\, the Portland Comedy 
 Festival\, the Burbank Comedy Festival and the San Leandro Comedy Festival
 .\n\n21+ Doors - 7p / Show - 8p $15adv / $20door\n\nCheck out **www.Barrel
 ProofLounge.com** for all sorts of good times ahead.
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/ira-summer-headlines-friday-night-comedy-
 downtown-santa-rosa-tickets-2002093221721?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
