DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T180000
UID:261128uuTcNA8Y5EiAlEalUXLw9Q
DESCRIPTION:Saturday afternoons hit differently at Barrel Proof Lounge.\n\
 nWe open early — 3pm — and hand the room over to Ukulele Ramblers\, a 
 friendly\, talented ukulele collective that turns Happy Hour into a laid-b
 ack\, sing-along hang.\n\nThis is live music and an open uke jam. Bring yo
 ur ukulele if you’ve got one. Bring your voice even if you don’t. The 
 Ramblers lead the way with familiar tunes\, easy harmonies\, and a welcomi
 ng vibe that makes it just as fun to join in as it is to sit back and list
 en.\n\nNo pressure. No ego. Just good songs\, good people\, and a room tha
 t feels like it belongs to everyone.\n\n Live Music & Open Uke Jam | 3–
 6pm  Happy Hour drinks  Free popcorn  21+\n\n Barrel Proof Lounge 501 
 Mendocino Avenue\, Downtown Santa Rosa\n\nIt’s the kind of afternoon you
  plan to stop by for one drink… and somehow stay for three hours.\n\n**w
 ww.UkuleleRamblers.net**\n\nCheck out **www.BarrelProofLounge.com** for al
 l sorts of good times ahead!
LOCATION:Barrel Proof Lounge
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/live-music-happy-hour-the-ukulele-rambler
 s-open-uke-jam-tickets-1485589782029?aff=oddtdtcreator
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“To Build a Fire\,” A Jack London Reading
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T153000
UID:261127nECfNfnWIUii5mrnlKT3mQ
DESCRIPTION:Gather in the warmth of the House of Happy Walls as Jeff Falco
 ner brings Jack London’s powerful storytelling to life through a live re
 ading of “To Build a Fire.” Experience the suspense\, vivid imagery\, 
 and chilling atmosphere of the Yukon as London’s words unfold. The readi
 ng will be followed by a discussion exploring the story’s themes and its
  lasting significance.  (This story addresses difficult topics and the ch
 allenges faced in survival situations. The material may be intense and is 
 not recommended for young children.)
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/to-build-a-fire/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Redwood Writers General Meeting  w/Korie Leigh: Write the Book You
  Need
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T133000
UID:261127Sm3PxNpFwUqUUx7S887ncA
DESCRIPTION:**Korie Leigh: Write the Book You Need**\n\n**Dec. 19\, 2026\,
  11 a.m. Finley Center in Santa Rosa**\n\nPlease bring something savory or
  sweet to share in our potluck!\n\n**“Write the Book You Need”** is a 
 **reflective and practical workshop for people who feel called to turn liv
 ed experience into meaningful writing.**\n\nDrawing from her work as an au
 thor\, clinician\, and educator\, Dr. Korie Leigh explores how personal st
 ories can become books that help readers feel seen\, supported\, or less a
 lone. Participants will learn how to identify the gap their story fills\, 
 move beyond memoir into broader reader impact\, and begin shaping experien
 ces into a book with purpose\, clarity\, and resonance.\n\n**About the Pre
 senter:**\n\n**Korie Leigh\, PhD\, FT\, CCLS\, is an award-winning author\
 , thanatologist\, certified child life specialist\, and Associate Professo
 r and Program Chair of Thanatology at Marian University.** She has spent m
 ore than twenty years supporting seriously ill and dying children and thei
 r families across pediatric hospitals\, oncology\, hospice\, palliative ca
 re\, and community settings.\n\nShe serves as Director of Psychosocial Ser
 vices and a board member at Hero’s Path Pediatric Palliative Care and ha
 s served as a childhood grief advisor to Sesame Workshop. She is the autho
 r of four traditionally published books with more than 22\,000 copies sold
 . **What Does Grief Feel Like?** (Free Spirit Publishing\, 2023) has sold 
 more than 10\,000 copies\, won a New Mexico Book Award\, appeared on Oprah
 ’s recommended reading list\, and had international rights purchased by 
 Indonesia’s Ministry of Education. It Won’t Ever Be the Same: A Teen
 ’s Guide to Grief and Grieving (Free Spirit Publishing\, 2024) has also 
 **sold more than 10\,000 copies and reached #1 on Amazon in the Teen & You
 ng Adult Grief category.**\n\nHer other titles are When Everything Changes
 : Parenting Through Loss and Grief (2026) and Why Are the Numbers All Jumb
 led? (2026). She lives in Santa Fe\, NM. Find Korie Leigh at **www.koriele
 ighphd.com.**
LOCATION:Finley Center
URL:https://redwoodwriters.org/dec-2026-korie-leigh/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pedal to the North Pole - on the Russian River Railbikes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T210000
UID:261124wwD9R9NYEUO_vtRj_i5nbA
DESCRIPTION:Pedal to the North Pole – A Christmas Railbike Adventure\n\n
 **December 18–28\, 2026 | Cloverdale\, California**\n\nMake this Christm
 as unforgettable with Pedal to the North Pole at Russian River Railbikes!\
 n\nFamilies and visitors are invited to experience a one-of-a-kind holiday
  adventure aboard custom-built railbikes. Pedal along historic railroad tr
 acks through the beautiful Sonoma County countryside\, while passing throu
 gh festively lit scenic forests. You will pass by a vineyard and travel th
 rough a historic railroad tunnel.\n\nThis special Christmas-season excursi
 on combines outdoor adventure\, railroad history\, and holiday excitement 
 for a memorable experience with family and friends.\n\nWhether you're look
 ing for a unique family outing\, a new holiday tradition\, or something di
 fferent to enjoy with visiting friends and relatives\, Pedal to the North 
 Pole offers a distinctive way to celebrate the season.\n\n**Holiday rides 
 begin December 18 and continue on select dates through December 28\, 2026.
 **\n\n**Reservations are recommended\, and holiday ride availability is li
 mited.**\n\n**BOOK YOUR CHRISTMAS ADVENTURE NOW!**\n\nVisit **www.russianr
 iverrailbikes.org** to view available rides and reserve your railbike.\n\n
 **Location:** Russian River Railbikes\, Cloverdale\, Sonoma County\, Calif
 ornia.
LOCATION:Russian River Railbikes
URL:http://www.russianriverrailbikes.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Discovering Women Poets\, a Poetry Competition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T235900
UID:261124VIp9RGe6BUq-91flKQsjQA
DESCRIPTION:The National League of American Pen Women \\(NLAPW\\) and the 
 Golden Gate-Marin Branch are launching a poetry competition for women over
  18 years of age who are not currently members of the NLAPW. This regional
  and national competition will be run at the Branch level in the semi-fina
 list phase. Local winners are automatically entered into the League’s Na
 tional competition.\n\nWinners at the Branch level will receive $35 and ha
 ve their entry published in the Branch newsletter. They will also be invit
 ed to present their poetry in person or by Zoom.\n\nBranch winners become 
 semi-finalists in the National competition\, which will award $100 to thre
 e winners. National winners will have their work and a short bio published
  in The Pen Woman\, a national magazine. All semi-finalists will be listed
  in the magazine.\n\nUp to three poems may be submitted for one entry fee 
 of $15. Each poem should be no longer than 40 lines. There are no restrict
 ions on topics or poem’s structure. Entries must be received by January 
 25\, 2027.\n\nDownload Entry Form at our website: https://www.goldengatema
 rinart.org/copy-of-contact
LOCATION:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org
URL:https://www.goldengatemarinart.org/copy-of-contact
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
